<section class="paper">
  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ My part</span>
      <h2>From the agency floor to the <span class="serif">field.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <p>I came onto Buck the Quo as an in-house creative at Drake Cooper, right at the start of it. I shot and cut the bulk of the photo and video and led the social team.</p>
      <p>When the campaign moved into the More In Store retail experience, my job changed. They put me in the field as a mentor to the teens, because of how I got here. I didn't go to college. I did an advertising internship that put me inside an agency in my early twenties, and they wanted me there to show teens that a future exists no matter what path they take.</p>
      <p>So I went from the main shooter, editor, and social lead to boots on the ground. Between 2015 and 2018 we had 18,000+ of those conversations. I mentored the ones chasing a media path: real conversations, connecting them to resources, and handing off the camera so they could shoot for the campaign themselves. The best of them became ambassadors who went out and made the work.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap did rv">
    <div class="bar">
